{"archive": {"commit": "8012191c69c75a008356ba7b7bd422f0d57d2884", "object_pointer": "/89", "path": "reports/sphere-eversion-history/commits-page-2.json", "sha256": "442e714c0b69b0d5d05337e84564e2ab859eab6298e1eec27e7eb08cf23d884e"}, "association_note": "The source explicitly states equivalence in finite dimensions and a problem in infinite dimensions; do not drop that qualification.", "dataset": "sphere-eversion", "excerpts": [{"field": "/commit/message", "text": "refactor(Immersion): replace by the proper definition of immersions\n(in finite dimensions)\n\nWe'd like immersions to be C^n; a smart constructor will not allow this\n(but differentiability at best). Hence, we need to also require smoothness.\n\nThe current definition of immersions is not the correct one in infinite-dimensional\nBanach manifolds. In finite dimensions, these are, however, equivalent."}], "id": "immersion-definition", "origin": "upstream_repository", "projects": [{"input_sha256": "4e72119aff81a0db29352a3b3a94606f738a1951fc06b66eef22ebe415d1052d", "project_id": "immersion-before", "relationship": "reported_subject", "root": "Immersion", "source_commit": "e7f4e9109e586404f4bf130e23e26ffd031f2459", "statement_applicability": "not_adjudicated"}, {"input_sha256": "df4beea7189458934f9048ea4fe92d6b0fb5e901ed034de90911f52c87e32ba6", "project_id": "immersion-after", "relationship": "reported_subject", "root": "Immersion", "source_commit": "27a2c7fdff78bb5509831699899796eaffe62a4b", "statement_applicability": "not_adjudicated"}], "schema_version": "paperlean-upstream-evidence-1", "source": {"author": "Michael Rothgang", "kind": "commit", "repository": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/sphere-eversion", "title": "refactor(Immersion): replace by the proper definition of immersions", "url": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/sphere-eversion/commit/27a2c7fdff78bb5509831699899796eaffe62a4b"}, "truth_status": "unverified_upstream_claim", "usable_as_scoring_label": false}
